{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And He said, I will return, etc.</b> He spoke in singular language, for one alone is the one giving the tidings, for the two — each one came for his own mission. And one must set the mind to why in the inquiry about Sarah two asked, while here [only] one spoke. Perhaps it is because since they also intended to inquire after her welfare through her husband, therefore all three asked, on account of the laws of proper conduct." "<b>I will certainly return, etc.</b> The reason for the doubling of <b>shov ashuv</b>, and also his saying the word <b>ve-hineh</b>, may intend to say in the manner of our Sages of blessed memory: when Yitzhak was born he was not fit to beget offspring, for he came from the side of the feminine (סִטְרָא דְּנוּקְבָּא), and through the act of the Binding (Akedah) he merited a soul fit to beget offspring. And this is what the angel alluded to in his statement <b>I will certainly return to you at this season, and behold, a son to Sarah</b> — meaning, from the side of the feminine. And it is precise to say ״וְהִנֵּה״ — meaning, that which presents itself beforehand is of this category. And he said <b>ashuv</b> — meaning, a second time He will return to him, meaning, to the aspect of Avraham, which is the world of the masculine (עָלְמָא דִּדְכוּרָא), and this was at the Binding, as it is written (Genesis 22:11): ״וַיִּקְרָא אֵלָיו מַלְאַךְ ה׳ מִן הַשָּׁמַיִם״ etc. And these are two visitations: one visitation — that Yitzhak would exist in the world; the second — that he would have a soul that generates offspring. And the reason HaShem did so is because of His saying (Genesis 17:19): ״לוּ יִשְׁמָעֵאל״, as I wrote there, and there are mysteries." "It further intends in His saying <b>and to Sarah a son</b> according to its plain sense, in the manner of our Sages of blessed memory (Vayikra Rabbah ch. 4): males always depend on females and females on males, as it is written (I Chronicles 4:18): ״וְאִשְׁתּוֹ הַיְהֻדִיָּה יָלְדָה אֶת יֶרֶד״; (Genesis 22:24): ״וּפִילַגְשׁוֹ וּשְׁמָהּ וְגוֹ׳ וַתֵּלֶד״ etc.; (Leviticus 12:2): ״אִשָּׁה כִּי תַזְרִיעַ וְיָלְדָה זָכָר״ — end quote. We too add to enumerate: a son to Sarah, etc." "<b>Now Sarah was listening.</b> The verse informs us that the tidings for Sarah were given by HaShem Himself in the mission, and that is its saying <b>Now Sarah was listening</b> etc. — and He Himself is the one giving tidings after him [the angel]. And I saw in the Midrash that even so the angel was punished for not having spoken the tidings directly to her from his own mouth but spoke to Avraham, for the angels are punished for an inadvertent error and for any deviation whatsoever."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:42:07.741807206Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}